{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B2ra6NViS51u2CUzxBrr7F","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: test-rel05.4\n     2→title: \"Test Suite: rel05.4 — md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum\"\n     3→release: rel05.4\n     4→\n     5→traces:\n     6→  - rel05.4-uc001-md5sum\n     7→  - rel05.4-uc002-sha1sum\n     8→  - rel05.4-uc003-sha256sum\n     9→  - rel05.4-uc004-sha512sum\n    10→  - prd030-md5sum R1\n    11→  - prd030-md5sum R2\n    12→  - prd031-sha1sum R1\n    13→  - prd031-sha1sum R2\n    14→  - prd032-sha256sum R1\n    15→  - prd032-sha256sum R2\n    16→  - prd033-sha512sum R1\n    17→  - prd033-sha512sum R2\n    18→\n    19→preconditions:\n    20→  - ./bin/md5sum, ./bin/sha1sum, ./bin/sha256sum, and ./bin/sha512sum exist (built via mage build).\n    21→  - Reference binaries gmd5sum, gsha1sum, gsha256sum, and gsha512sum are installed via Homebrew (coreutils) and on PATH.\n    22→  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/md5sum/... ./cmd/sha1sum/... ./cmd/sha256sum/... ./cmd/sha512sum/... which invoke RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n    23→  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n    24→  - No normalization is applied; all outputs are compared byte-for-byte.\n    25→  - Test setup creates a known file (e.g. containing \"hello\\n\") and a pre-computed checksum file for check-mode tests.\n    26→\n    27→test_cases:\n    28→\n    29→  # ---- md5sum ----\n    30→\n    31→  - name: md5sum_compute_stdin\n    32→    description: Compute MD5 of stdin; output is \"HASH  -\" in GNU text format.\n    33→    inputs:\n    34→      args: []\n    35→      stdin: \"hello\\n\"\n    36→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    37→    normalization: none\n    38→    expected:\n    39→      exit_code: 0\n    40→      stdout: \"b1946ac92492d2347c6235b4d2611184  -\\n\"\n    41→      stderr: \"\"\n    42→    traces:\n    43→      - prd030-md5sum R1.1\n    44→      - prd030-md5sum R1.2\n    45→\n    46→  - name: md5sum_compute_file\n    47→    description: \"Compute MD5 of a named file. Setup: hello.txt contains 'hello\\\\n'.\"\n    48→    inputs:\n    49→      args: [\"hello.txt\"]\n    50→      stdin: null\n    51→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    52→    normalization: none\n    53→    expected:\n    54→      exit_code: 0\n    55→      stdout: \"b1946ac92492d2347c6235b4d2611184  hello.txt\\n\"\n    56→      stderr: \"\"\n    57→    traces:\n    58→      - prd030-md5sum R1.1\n    59→\n    60→  - name: md5sum_binary_mode\n    61→    description: \"-b uses asterisk format: 'HASH *FILENAME'.\"\n    62→    inputs:\n    63→      args: [\"-b\", \"hello.txt\"]\n    64→      stdin: null\n    65→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    66→    normalization: none\n    67→    expected:\n    68→      exit_code: 0\n    69→      stdout: \"b1946ac92492d2347c6235b4d2611184 *hello.txt\\n\"\n    70→      stderr: \"\"\n    71→    traces:\n    72→      - prd030-md5sum R3.1\n    73→\n    74→  - name: md5sum_tag_format\n    75→    description: \"--tag uses BSD format: 'MD5 (FILENAME) = HASH'.\"\n    76→    inputs:\n    77→      args: [\"--tag\", \"hello.txt\"]\n    78→      stdin: null\n    79→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    80→    normalization: none\n    81→    expected:\n    82→      exit_code: 0\n    83→      stdout: \"MD5 (hello.txt) = b1946ac92492d2347c6235b4d2611184\\n\"\n    84→      stderr: \"\"\n    85→    traces:\n    86→      - prd030-md5sum R1.3\n    87→\n    88→  - name: md5sum_check_valid\n    89→    description: \"--check on a valid checksum file exits 0 and prints OK. Setup: checksums.md5 contains the correct hash for hello.txt.\"\n    90→    inputs:\n    91→      args: [\"--check\", \"checksums.md5\"]\n    92→      stdin: null\n    93→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    94→    normalization: none\n    95→    expected:\n    96→      exit_code: 0\n    97→      stdout: \"hello.txt: OK\\n\"\n    98→      stderr: \"\"\n    99→    traces:\n   100→      - prd030-md5sum R2.1\n   101→      - prd030-md5sum R2.2\n  